{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. You’re in the ICU because your blood sugar was extremely high and you were in diabetic ketoacidosis. Do you remember calling your kids to call an ambulance?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes… I knew something was wrong. I hadn’t taken my fast-acting insulin for a few days. I was drinking a lot and just… didn’t care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Your glucose was 830 when you arrived, and your body was producing ketones. We started an insulin drip and fluids to correct that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt so thirsty and my heart was racing. I knew it was DKA again. I’m sorry this keeps happening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not here to judge. We want to help you get better and prevent this from happening again. You also had very high potassium, which can be dangerous for the heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "High potassium? I didn’t know that could happen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, in DKA, acidosis shifts potassium out of cells. Your EKG showed changes, so we gave calcium to protect your heart and are watching it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is my heart okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your troponin was slightly elevated, likely from stress on the heart during DKA, not a heart attack. It’s improving now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. My kidneys too—they said my creatinine was high?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your creatinine was 1.9, but it’s likely due to dehydration from DKA. We call that pre-renal azotemia. With fluids, it’s already improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t been drinking much water. Just vodka."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve started you on IV fluids and thiamine, folic acid, and multivitamins because heavy drinking can deplete those."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been trying to cut down. I’m in an outpatient program, but I slipped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s honest. We’re not restarting naltrexone for now since you haven’t been taking it consistently. We’ll discuss that with your PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I do want help. I know my depression and drinking are messing with my diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2163-04-08 17:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a great step. We’ll make sure you have follow-up with your doctor and a mental health provider."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2163-04-09 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood sugar is coming down—239 this morning. The insulin drip is being adjusted."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2163-04-09 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s better than 800. When will I be off the drip?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2163-04-09 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Once your acidosis resolves and you can eat, we’ll switch you to injections. Your anion gap is closing, which is great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2163-04-09 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling less shaky. Can I eat something?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2163-04-09 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start you on a light diet. Also, your platelet count is low, which we’re watching. It could be from alcohol or liver issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2163-04-09 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2163-04-09 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now, but your PCP should check your liver function. We’re holding acetaminophen for now just to be safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2163-04-09 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll follow up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2163-04-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Your creatinine is down to 0.9, and potassium is stable. We’re switching you to the floor today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2163-04-10 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about my insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2163-04-10 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be on Lantus 28 units in the morning and Humalog 7 units before meals. A diabetes educator will review it with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2163-04-10 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s less Lantus than before. Why?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2163-04-10 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because your sugars are stabilizing. We’ll adjust based on your readings. Your A1c was 11%, so we know control has been tough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2163-04-10 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. I need better support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2163-04-10 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We agree. Social work will help connect you with resources, and you should talk to your doctor about counseling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2163-04-11 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are looking good. Glucose is 148, bicarbonate is 23. You’re almost ready for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2163-04-11 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so much better. No more thirst or racing heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2163-04-11 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll make sure you have all your medications, including sertraline and your blood pressure pills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2163-04-11 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been taking the sertraline. It helps, but I still drink when I’m down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2163-04-11 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. The key is linking mental health and diabetes care. Your PCP can help coordinate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2163-04-11 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make that appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s the day. You’re being discharged. Your vitals are stable, and labs are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember: take your insulin, avoid alcohol, and follow up with your doctor within a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll talk to them about counseling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. We also gave you a vaginal cream for a yeast infection—use it for four nights."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t know I had that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s common with high blood sugar. It should clear up now that your glucose is controlled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Any other warnings?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you feel short of breath, chest pain, or your blood sugar goes very high again, come back right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I don’t want to be back here soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t either. Take care of yourself. Your team is here to support you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try my best. Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Discharge papers are ready. Nurse will go over them with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll listen carefully."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your blood pressure is good now, so we restarted losartan and amlodipine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll take them every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. And keep taking ferrous sulfate for your iron levels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I sometimes forget, but I’ll set a reminder."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good idea. Small steps make a big difference."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to make changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad to hear that. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again. I appreciate your patience."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Stay healthy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in shortly to finalize discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, and don’t hesitate to reach out if you need help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2163-04-12 08:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2163-04-08 16:37:00",
    "admission_end": "2163-04-12 17:52:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of poorly controlled type 1 diabetes, alcohol abuse, and depression was admitted after presenting with diabetic ketoacidosis due to missed insulin and heavy alcohol use. She had severe hyperglycemia, anion gap metabolic acidosis, hyperkalemia, and acute kidney injury likely from hypovolemia. She was treated in the ICU with IV fluids, insulin drip, and calcium for hyperkalemia. Her condition stabilized, and she was transitioned to subcutaneous insulin. Her renal function improved, and she was discharged with a revised insulin regimen, continuation of chronic medications, and instructions to follow up with her primary care provider for mental health and liver evaluation. She acknowledged the need for better adherence and agreed to seek counseling.",
    "problems": [
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with ketoacidosis without coma",
      "Alcohol abuse with intoxication, unspecified",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Hyperkalemia",
      "Hypovolemia",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Long term (current) use of insulin",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Other secondary thrombocytopenia",
      "Patient's other noncompliance with medication regimen"
    ]
  }
}
